 Four previous hospital visits are retained. Current acute findings must not be backdated into earlier encounters.\nRecorded acuity: Critical at this synthetic assessment: Sudden dyspnoea, reduced prosthetic sounds and documented subtherapeutic INR. BP 90/60 mmHg, pulse 126/min, SpO₂ 86% on room air. Supporting results: INR 1.4 ratio; Lactate 3.8 mmol/L; Creatinine 1.5 mg/dL. Senior assessment is required; a working-list entry does not mean readiness.\nHistory source and context: Spouse provides history and keeps a folder of reports; home medicines still need verification.\nAvailable results: INR 1.4 ratio; Lactate 3.8 mmol/L; Creatinine 1.5 mg/dL; Haemoglobin 12.8 g/dL; Albumin 3.1 g/dL.\nAssessment is a synthetic authored scenario, not an AI diagnosis. Senior team assessment is documented. Acute resuscitation, administration records and full critical-care charting are intentionally not represented; this is not a complete treatment record.","source_ids":["00000042-0000-4000-8000-000000056005"],"source_system":"MockHIS"},{"id":"00000059-0000-4000-8000-000000056001","hospital_id":"10000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001","patient_id":"20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000056","encounter_id":"00000041-0000-4000-8000-000000056005","kind":"progress","recorded_at":"2026-09-08T07:00:00.000Z","author":"Dr. Rohan Shah","title":"Ward round — current admission review","body":"Findings: Sudden dyspnoea, reduced prosthetic sounds and documented subtherapeutic INR. Critical at this synthetic assessment: Sudden dyspnoea, reduced prosthetic sounds and documented subtherapeutic INR. BP 90/60 mmHg, pulse 126/min, SpO₂ 86% on room air. Supporting results: INR 1.4 ratio; Lactate 3.8 mmol/L; Creatinine 1.5 mg/dL. Senior assessment is required; a working-list entry does not mean readiness.\nPlan: Review systemic findings and document discrepancies in the anticoagulation history. Pending: Repeat INR result and source review; Internal Medicine assessment and documented response; Senior review of